<%#
  ENGINE STATUS (studio-engine 0.113.0.rc1, measured 2026-10-24
  (turf-readopts-engine-modals)): KEPT. This card hands the address back to the
  caller (props.onSubmit) and posts nothing; the engine's newsletter-email posts
  its own form. The engine newsletter modals (studio/profiles/_newsletter_modals)
  are NOT a drop-in:
    - they answer to $store.profileModals, not the app host's $store.modals;
    - they post a plain form (turbo off, full reload) to the engine's
      profile_newsletter_path, while this app posts JSON to its own
      newsletter_subscribe_path / newsletter_unsubscribe_path and applies the
      25-seed StateFanout and the newsletter-state-changed event in place;
    - they register only newsletter-email and newsletter-unsubscribe: the engine
      has no subscribe card with a consent box, no Subscribed! beat and no goodbye
      beat, and its copy differs.
  Engine follow-up: newsletter modals that take modal_store, a JSON submit mode
  with a success hook, and optional subscribe / success / goodbye cards with
  app copy. Until then this card stays here.
%>
<%# Web3 email-capture modal — opened by the questNewsletter factory via
    $store.modals.open('newsletter-email', { onSubmit: fn }). Captures the email
    (web3 users have none on file), closes itself, then hands the address back to
    onSubmit, which POSTs the subscribe. Single root (the host mounts this through
    its own template x-if); props reader + submit defined inline, no factory. %>
<div x-data="{
       email: '',
       get props() { return ($store.modals.current() || {}).props || {} },
       submit() {
         var em = (this.email || '').trim();
         if (em.indexOf('@') < 1) return;
         var cb = this.props.onSubmit;
         $store.modals.close();
         if (cb) cb(em);
       }
     }">
  <%= render 'studio/modals/blocks/card_header', size: :md, icon_emoji: '📬', title: 'One more thing' do %>
    Drop your email to join the list and claim your 25 seeds. We only use it for the newsletter.
  <% end %>
  <div class="px-5 pb-5">
    <input type="email" x-model="email" @keydown.enter.prevent="submit()"
           placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email"
           class="w-full bg-inset border border-subtle rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm text-heading mb-3 focus:border-primary/50 focus:outline-none">
    <button type="button" @click="submit()" class="btn btn-primary w-full">Join &amp; Claim 25 Seeds</button>
  </div>
</div>
